0:{"buildId":"7afh9cBoHBO9HIwX4Lcyt","data":[{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","$L2",null,{"toc":[{"depth":2,"url":"#there-is-no-actionscheduler-trait","title":["No ",["$","code",null,{"children":"ActionScheduler"}]," trait exists"]},{"depth":2,"url":"#when-are-two-actions-the-same-action","title":"When are two actions the same action?"},{"depth":2,"url":"#ordering-is-one-64-bit-integer","title":"Ordering is one 64-bit integer"},{"depth":2,"url":"#two-state-enums-and-one-that-never-appears","title":"Two state enums, and one that never appears"},{"depth":2,"url":"#matching-is-first-fit-over-an-lru","title":"Matching is first-fit over an LRU"},{"depth":3,"url":"#platform-properties-are-typed-and-minimum-is-a-resource-pool","title":["Platform properties are typed, and ",["$","code",null,{"children":"Minimum"}]," is a resource pool"]},{"depth":2,"url":"#retries-and-what-failed-means","title":"Retries, and what \"failed\" means"},{"depth":3,"url":"#two-timeouts-with-very-different-defaults","title":"Two timeouts with very different defaults"},{"depth":2,"url":"#who-writes-the-action-cache-entry","title":"Who writes the action cache entry?"},{"depth":2,"url":"#where-the-exact-truth-lives","title":"Where the exact truth lives"},{"depth":2,"url":"#common-questions","title":"Common questions"}],"children":[["$","$L3",null,{"children":"Scheduler internals"}],["$","$L4",null,{"children":"Action merging, the awaited-action database, how a worker is chosen, and what happens when an action fails."}],["$","$L5",null,{"children":["\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Who this is for:"}]," anyone tuning a scheduler, debugging an action that\nqueued forever, or wondering why two identical builds did not share work.\n",["$","strong",null,{"children":"What you'll have at the end:"}]," the merge rule, the ordering rule, the\nmatching rule, and the retry rule, each of which has at least one\ncounter-intuitive edge. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"Time:"}]," twenty-five minutes."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"The scheduler's job sounds small: take actions from clients, give them to\nworkers. Almost all of its complexity comes from three questions it has to\nanswer that the protocol does not specify: when are two actions the same\none, which of the queued actions goes next, and what does \"this failed\" mean."}],"\n",["$","$L6",null,{"as":"h2","id":"there-is-no-actionscheduler-trait","children":["No ",["$","code",null,{"children":"ActionScheduler"}]," trait exists"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["If you go looking for one (and older material about Forge will send you\nlooking) you will not find it. The abstraction is split by ",["$","em",null,{"children":"who is asking"}],",\ninto three traits in\n",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://github.com/toxicwind/forge/blob/v1.6.5/forge-util/src/operation_state_manager.rs","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","data-source-link":"forge-util/src/operation_state_manager.rs","data-source-ref":"v1.6.5","title":"forge-util/src/operation_state_manager.rs at v1.6.5","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-md border border-border bg-surface-elevated px-1.5 py-0.5 align-middle font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground no-underline transition-colors hover:border-brand/50 hover:text-brand","children":[["$","svg",null,{"width":"12","height":"12","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","aria-hidden":"true","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"m16 18 6-6-6-6M8 6l-6 6 6 6"}]}],"operation_state_manager.rs"]}],":"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"ClientStateManager"}]}]," is the client's view: submit an action, subscribe to\nits progress. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"WorkerStateManager"}]}]," is the worker's view: report that an\noperation changed state. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"MatchingEngineStateManager"}]}]," is the matcher's\nview: list actions that could be dispatched, assign one to a worker."]}],"\n","$L7","\n","$L8","\n","$L9","\n","$La","\n","$Lb","\n","$Lc","\n","$Ld","\n","$Le","\n","$Lf","\n","$L10","\n","$L11","\n","$L12","\n","$L13","\n","$L14","\n","$L15","\n","$L16","\n","$L17","\n","$L18","\n","$L19","\n","$L1a","\n","$L1b","\n","$L1c","\n","$L1d","\n","$L1e","\n","$L1f","\n","$L20","\n","$L21","\n","$L22","\n","$L23","\n","$L24","\n","$L25","\n","$L26","\n","$L27","\n","$L28","\n","$L29","\n","$L2a","\n","$L2b","\n","$L2c","\n","$L2d","\n","$L2e","\n","$L2f","\n","$L30","\n","$L31","\n","$L32","\n","$L33","\n","$L34","\n","$L35","\n","$L36","\n","$L37","\n","$L38","\n","$L39","\n","$L3a","\n","$L3b","\n","$L3c"]}],"$L3d"]}],["$L3e","$L3f"],"$L40"]}],"isPartial":"$@41","staleTime":"$42","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$L43","isPartial":"$@44","staleTime":"$42","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$L45","isPartial":"$@46","staleTime":"$42","varyParams":"$47"}],"isUpgradeableISRFallback":false,"a":"$@48","rootVaryParams":null,"needsRuntimeRequest":"$@49"}
